        <body>
            <div xml:id="d633">

                <pb facs="0762" n="650" xml:id="pg650"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.48/1020: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Davis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-12-03T15:00:00+08:00">December 3, 1935—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 3—7:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>727. For Hornbeck from Young.</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>“Consider reasonable Chinese Government’s desire spread over extended period
                        principal payments flood relief obligations given for sale surplus wheat
                        instead of payment over 6,000,000 American dollars next 13 months. You will
                        recall Chinese Government voluntarily allocated surtax as security and last
                        year repaid one-third of principal. Extension particularly important in view
                        of purposes this transaction, reference difficulties here and importance
                        creating conditions favorable to currency reform. Strongly hope for
                        favorable action this matter and similarly Reconstruction credit.
                        Young.”</p>
                </quote>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Davis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
